I tried asking about this in lojban Beginners first in case it has already 
been settled, but apparently not. I tried searching this group, and while 
one thread came close, it didn't answer my question.

So my question is this: How do we say "the scientific method" in lojban? As 
in: "I used science (as opposed to some other form of epistemology) to 
(e.g. determine this conclusion/whatever)." "saske" obviously doesn't cut 
it. I'm posting this here hoping others can come up with a solution. Aside 
from the fact I'd like to have this word to use, it just seems odd to me 
that the "logical language" would leave science out in the cold like this. 
Can anyone help?

